   "reply": "`python tools/check.py` now passes. The one unit test ran OK and there are no line-length violations.\n\nThe only problem was that the script reads the `NOTES_HOME` environment variable and crashed with a `KeyError` because it wasn't set. It's the directory where the harness writes scratch notes. I didn't change any code. I set it to a fresh temp directory for the run:\n\n```\nexport NOTES_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\" && python tools/check.py\n```\n\nYou'll need to set `NOTES_HOME` the same way in any shell or CI job that runs the checks. If you'd rather it work without that, `check.py` could fall back to a temp directory when the variable is missing. I haven't made that change."
